HST Office: a 1280 px window shows the full banner.

The banner switches to its compact artwork below 1280 px of window width, but it measured the system
window, the client area, which the frame keeps 12 px narrower with gtk3 (the resize borders on Windows):
at exactly 1280 px every app showed the compact banner. The width now includes a 16 px frame allowance.

- sfx2/source/notebookbar/NotebookbarTabControl.cxx.

License: these upstream files remain under their original license (MPL-2.0).
---
--- a/sfx2/source/notebookbar/NotebookbarTabControl.cxx
+++ b/sfx2/source/notebookbar/NotebookbarTabControl.cxx
@@ -448,7 +448,11 @@
                                        GetOutputSizePixel().Width() - 2 * aPos.X(),
                                        pPage->GetSizePixel().Height() };
         const vcl::Window* pTop = GetSystemWindow();
-        const tools::Long nWindowWidth = pTop ? pTop->GetSizePixel().Width() : GetSizePixel().Width();
+        // the 1280 px threshold is the window's outer width; the system window is its client area,
+        // which the frame keeps narrower (12 px with gtk3, the resize borders on Windows): add a
+        // frame allowance, or a 1280 px window shows the compact banner
+        const tools::Long nWindowWidth = (pTop ? pTop->GetSizePixel().Width() : GetSizePixel().Width())
+                                         + std::lround(16 * fDpi);
         tools::Long nPageWidth = aPage.w;
         const hst::banner::Mode eMode = hst::banner::modeFor(nWindowWidth, aPage.h, fDpi);
         if (eMode != hst::banner::Mode::Hidden)
